{
 "figure": "f11_connected_boundary",
 "evidence_label": "3: computer-assisted proof; displayed polylines are endpoint midpoint guides",
 "alt_text": "The original period18 orbit is joined to a saddle-node at fixed output rate. A107-chart native plus-one locus joins that fold to a generic1:1 resonance. The resonance has exactly two unit multipliers and eleven strictly attracting complementary modes.",
 "notes": "Endpoint boxes and proper full-state joins come from independent saved384-bit arithmetic. No line is interpolated across the change of gauge. Lines inside each group guide the eye; they are not polygonal interval enclosures. Spectrum dots locate Gershgorin centers; true enclosure radii are drawn but mostly below image resolution. Attraction is proved on the green cross-section, not claimed along the whole grey line or blue locus.",
